    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d191">

                <pb facs="0383" n="1343" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1343"/>

                <head>No. 904.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. de
                        Weckherlin.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-06-06"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 6,
                        1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your note of the 9th ultimo,
                    in relation to the tonnage dues collected at New York in April last from the
                    Dutch steamer <hi rendition="#italic">Prins Maurits</hi>, I now have the honor
                    to transmit to you for your information a copy of a letter from the Secretary of
                    the Treasury relative to the subject.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>



